OL,3,GNorthern Ireland
OL,4,
OL,5,CToday:FA dry start in south and east,
OL,6,Fbut occasionally heavy showers in
OL,7,Fnorth and west spreading across most
OL,8,Fareas, with the chance of thunder,
OL,9,Fshowers may become slow to move away.
OL,10,
OL,11,CTonight:FHeavier showers dying out
OL,12,Fthrough the evening but some
OL,13,Fcontinuing through the night, perhaps
OL,14,Fdrier in the south, feeling cooler
OL,15,Fwith freshening northeasterly winds.
OL,16,
OL,17,CThursday:FQuite breezy and feeling
OL,18,Ffresher with some showers, these
OL,19,Fmostly light and moving away quite
OL,20,Fbriskly.
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
